    {
      "cn_text": "首席研究作者林肯·泰兹表示，自2006年起，一些科学家提出植物拥有类似神经元的细胞，这些细胞与激素和神经递质相互作用，形成「类似于动物的植物神经系统」，「他们甚至声称植物根尖处存在「类似大脑的指挥中心」。」",
      "en_text": "Beginning in 2006, some scientists have argued that plants possess neuron-like cells that interact with hormones and neurotransmitters, forming “a plant nervous system, analogous to that in animals,” said lead study author Lincoln Taiz, “They even claimed that plants have ‘brain-like command centers’ at their root tips.”",
      "id": 2022013005,
      "order_seq": "content_3_1",
      "task_id": 202201001,
